        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">The Buddha</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">6th or 5th century BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">Traditionally at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lumbini">Lumbini</a>, now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, in the Shakya clan, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suddhodana">Śuddhodana</a>; dates uncertain, 563–483 BCE in much early 20th-century scholarship</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">Traditionally at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushinagar">Kushinagar</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, aged about eighty, reaching <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parinirvana">parinirvana</a>; the year is disputed</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Wandering religious teacher and founder of the saṅgha; held by Buddhists to be the Awakened One, described by historians as a śramaṇa teacher</span></div>
